{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> There is no earlier and later in the Torah; its meaning is 'and He had already said.' So too, <b>and YHWH Elohim caused to spring up</b> (Genesis 2). And many like these. Now, when he returned Jethro's flocks to him, HaShem promised him that he would go to Egypt without fear, for Pharaoh and his servants who knew the matter of the Egyptian had died. This is <b>'and the king of Egypt died'</b> (above, 2:23), for as long as he was alive, Moses was not fit to be an emissary to Pharaoh."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:36.467177224Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}